---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stack Scale — AI Adoption & Enablement | Stack10"
  description="You've deployed AI tools. Your team still isn't using them. Stack Scale measures adoption at 30, 60, and 90 days — and gives you the data to prove behavioural change to the board."
  canonicalUrl="https://stack10.ai/services/scale/"
>

  <!-- ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="svc-hero hero-dark">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-hero-inner animate-fade-up">
        <span class="section-label svc-hero-label">Stack Scale</span>
        <h1 class="svc-hero-title">AI deployed. Now prove your team is actually using it.</h1>
        <p class="svc-hero-subtitle">Most organisations have already spent on AI tools. The hard part isn't access — it's adoption. Stack Scale measures behavioural change at 30, 60, and 90 days so you have something real to report to the board.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            Book a Discovery Call
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7"/><path d="M7 7h10v10"/></svg>
          </a>
          <a href="/services/build/" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">See Stack Build</a>
        </div>
        <p class="svc-hero-note">Stack Scale runs standalone or as the final phase after Stack Build — whichever fits where you are now.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── PAIN SECTION ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section svc-pain-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">Sound familiar?</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">The adoption problem most organisations can't see clearly</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">If any of these are true, the issue isn't the tools. It's adoption.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-pain-grid">
        <div class="card svc-pain-card">
          <div class="svc-pain-number">01</div>
          <h3 class="svc-pain-heading">The tools are deployed. The habits aren't.</h3>
          <p class="svc-pain-body">You rolled out Copilot, ChatGPT Enterprise, or a custom AI tool six months ago. Uptake was high in week one. By week six, your team had reverted to the way they always worked. The licences are running. The workflows aren't.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card svc-pain-card">
          <div class="svc-pain-number">02</div>
          <h3 class="svc-pain-heading">Leadership and operations are on different planets.</h3>
          <p class="svc-pain-body">Your executives are enthusiastic about AI in strategy sessions. Your operations teams see it as extra work, a compliance risk, or just noise. Without a shared language and governance model, the gap widens — and nothing embeds.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card svc-pain-card">
          <div class="svc-pain-number">03</div>
          <h3 class="svc-pain-heading">The board is asking what changed.</h3>
          <p class="svc-pain-body">You've spent on AI. Now you need to show something for it. "We ran training sessions" isn't an answer. You need adoption rates, productivity delta, governance compliance — data that holds up in a board pack, not anecdotes from a workshop.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── ENGAGEMENT FORMATS ────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">Engagement formats</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Two ways to engage</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Start at the leadership level or run a full organisation-wide adoption program. Both formats have measurable outcomes — contact us for pricing.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc-tiers">

        <div class="card svc-tier">
          <div class="svc-tier-header">
            <div>
              <h3 class="svc-tier-name">Executive AI Briefing</h3>
              <p class="svc-tier-tagline">Half a day with your leadership team. Walk out aligned on strategy, governance, and what AI actually means for your organisation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="svc-tier-pricing">
              <span class="svc-tier-duration">Half-day</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="svc-tier-list">
            <li>Leadership alignment on AI strategy and priorities</li>
            <li>Strategic framing and opportunity mapping</li>
            <li>AI governance and responsible use overview</li>
            <li>Q&amp;A and facilitated next-steps</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="svc-tier-note">A common first step — especially when leadership is not yet aligned before a broader rollout begins.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card svc-tier svc-tier-featured">
          <div class="svc-tier-badge-wrap">
            <span class="badge badge-success">Full organisation transformation</span>
          </div>
          <div class="svc-tier-header">
            <div>
              <h3 class="svc-tier-name">AI Adoption Program</h3>
              <p class="svc-tier-tagline">90 days. Role-specific training, department AI Champions, custom playbooks, and adoption measured at three checkpoints — not just at the end.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="svc-tier-pricing">
              <span class="svc-tier-duration">90-day program</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="svc-tier-list">
            <li>Role-specific, hands-on training by department</li>
            <li>AI Champions built and activated across your org</li>
            <li>Custom AI playbooks by role and workflow</li>
            <li>Adoption measured at 30, 60, and 90 days</li>
            <li>Board-ready outcome report at program close</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── 30/60/90 MEASUREMENT ──────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">The accountability framework</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">We don't measure training completion. We measure what changed.</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Anyone can hand your team a certificate. We give you a structured 90-day measurement cadence that tracks real behavioural change — and intervenes when it's not happening fast enough.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc-timeline">
        <div class="svc-timeline-track" aria-hidden="true"></div>

        <div class="svc-timeline-item">
          <div class="svc-timeline-marker">
            <span class="svc-timeline-day">Day 30</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card svc-measure-card">
            <h3 class="svc-measure-heading">Early adoption signals</h3>
            <p class="svc-measure-body">Usage data, workflow integration rates, and early champion activity are reviewed against baseline. We identify the quick-win gaps and act immediately — not at the end.</p>
            <ul class="svc-measure-metrics">
              <li>Tool usage rates vs. pre-program baseline</li>
              <li>Champion activation by department</li>
              <li>Early friction points and blockers</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="svc-timeline-item">
          <div class="svc-timeline-marker">
            <span class="svc-timeline-day">Day 60</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card svc-measure-card">
            <h3 class="svc-measure-heading">Embedding and adjustment</h3>
            <p class="svc-measure-body">Role-specific adoption gaps are addressed. Champion activity is benchmarked against target. Playbooks are refined based on what's actually working inside your organisation — not what worked somewhere else.</p>
            <ul class="svc-measure-metrics">
              <li>Role-specific adoption gap analysis</li>
              <li>Playbook refinement and redeployment</li>
              <li>Champion performance benchmarking</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="svc-timeline-item">
          <div class="svc-timeline-marker">
            <span class="svc-timeline-day">Day 90</span>
          </div>
          <div class="card svc-measure-card svc-measure-card-final">
            <h3 class="svc-measure-heading">Validated outcomes</h3>
            <p class="svc-measure-body">Full program review against the baseline metrics set on day one. Adoption rates, productivity delta, and governance compliance are reported with data — ready for your board, not dressed up for it.</p>
            <ul class="svc-measure-metrics">
              <li>Adoption rate vs. target</li>
              <li>Productivity delta by role and department</li>
              <li>Governance compliance status</li>
              <li>Board-ready outcome report</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="svc-measure-callout">
        <p class="svc-measure-callout-text">The difference between Stack Scale and a training vendor: at day 90 you have a data set, not a participant list.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CAPABILITIES ──────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-muted">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-caps-grid">
        <div class="svc-caps-copy">
          <span class="section-label">What we deliver</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Capabilities</h2>
          <p class="section-desc">Stack Scale covers the full adoption lifecycle — from executive alignment to embedded daily workflows. Every engagement includes governance so it doesn't just stick, it sticks safely.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="svc-caps-list">
          <li class="svc-caps-item">
            <span class="svc-caps-marker" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>Executive AI briefing and leadership alignment</span>
          </li>
          <li class="svc-caps-item">
            <span class="svc-caps-marker" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>AI Adoption Program — role-specific, hands-on, 90-day measured</span>
          </li>
          <li class="svc-caps-item">
            <span class="svc-caps-marker" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>AI Champions — internal advocates built by department</span>
          </li>
          <li class="svc-caps-item">
            <span class="svc-caps-marker" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>Custom AI playbooks by role and function</span>
          </li>
          <li class="svc-caps-item">
            <span class="svc-caps-marker" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>AI governance and responsible use policy</span>
          </li>
          <li class="svc-caps-item">
            <span class="svc-caps-marker" aria-hidden="true">—</span>
            <span>Board-ready reporting at 30, 60, and 90 days</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── RIGHT FOR YOU IF ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-fit-grid">
        <div class="svc-fit-copy">
          <span class="section-label">Is this right for you?</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Stack Scale is the right engagement if&hellip;</h2>
          <p class="svc-fit-sub">These aren't hypothetical scenarios. They're the situations we hear most from CTOs, COOs, and CPOs at Australian mid-market businesses.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card svc-fit-box">
          <ul class="svc-fit-list">
            <li class="svc-fit-item">
              <svg class="svc-fit-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
              <span>You deployed Copilot, ChatGPT Enterprise, or a similar tool — and six months later your team is still working the same way they always did</span>
            </li>
            <li class="svc-fit-item">
              <svg class="svc-fit-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
              <span>Your leadership team and operations teams are not aligned on what AI is for, who owns it, or what the governance boundaries are</span>
            </li>
            <li class="svc-fit-item">
              <svg class="svc-fit-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
              <span>The board has asked what your AI investment actually changed — and you don't have a data-backed answer yet</span>
            </li>
            <li class="svc-fit-item">
              <svg class="svc-fit-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
              <span>You need a governance framework in place before AI can proceed at scale — and you want adoption and governance handled together, not separately</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section section-dark-block">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-cta-inner">
        <span class="section-label svc-cta-label">The training that sticks</span>
        <h2 class="svc-cta-title">"But training never sticks."<br>We know. That's why we measure it.</h2>
        <p class="svc-cta-desc">Stack Scale isn't a training program. It's an accountability program with training inside it. The 30/60/90 measurement cadence exists specifically because behaviour doesn't change from a single session. We follow through — and we give you the data to prove it did.</p>
        <div class="svc-cta-actions">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            Book a Discovery Call
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7"/><path d="M7 7h10v10"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── RELATED ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="svc-related-header">
        <span class="section-label">The full picture</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Stack Scale in context</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">Stack Scale runs standalone — for organisations that have already deployed AI tools and need adoption support. It also runs as the final phase after Stack Build, once custom AI systems are live and need to be embedded into daily workflows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-related-cards">
        <a href="/services/build/" class="card card-clickable svc-related-card">
          <div class="svc-related-card-tag">
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Upstream</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="svc-related-card-title">Stack Build</h3>
          <p class="svc-related-card-desc">Senior AI engineers building production AI systems on story-point pricing. From validated opportunity to deployed software — Stack Scale picks up where Build leaves off.</p>
          <span class="svc-related-card-link">
            Learn about Stack Build
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </a>
        <a href="/services/discover/" class="card card-clickable svc-related-card">
          <div class="svc-related-card-tag">
            <span class="badge badge-secondary">Before you build</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="svc-related-card-title">Stack Discover</h3>
          <p class="svc-related-card-desc">Not sure which AI opportunities are worth pursuing first? Stack Discover identifies and validates the highest-value AI use cases in your business before any budget is committed to build.</p>
          <span class="svc-related-card-link">
            Learn about Stack Discover
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .svc-hero {
    background: var(--gray-1000);
    color: var(--gray-50);
    padding: var(--space-24) 0 var(--space-20);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gray-800);
  }

  .svc-hero-inner {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .svc-hero-label {
    color: var(--green-400);
    border-color: oklch(0.76 0.21 150 / 0.3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5.5vw, var(--size-6xl));
    font-weight: var(--weight-800);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--gray-0);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-hero-subtitle {
    font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2vw, var(--size-xl));
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    color: var(--gray-400);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .svc-hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-hero-note {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--gray-500);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Pain section ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .svc-pain-section {
    background: var(--background);
  }

  .svc-pain-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-pain-card {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--border);
    border-top-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .svc-pain-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .svc-pain-heading {
    font-size: var(--size-xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .svc-pain-body {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Engagement tiers ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .svc-tiers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-tier {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .svc-tier-featured {
    border-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .svc-tier-badge-wrap {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space-3) * -1);
  }

  .svc-tier-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .svc-tier-name {
    font-size: var(--size-2xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-1);
  }

  .svc-tier-tagline {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .svc-tier-pricing {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  .svc-tier-price {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-3xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .svc-tier-duration {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  .svc-tier-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .svc-tier-list li {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    position: relative;
  }

  .svc-tier-list li::before {
    content: "✓";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
  }

  .svc-tier-note {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── 30/60/90 Timeline ────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .svc-timeline {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .svc-timeline-track {
    display: none;
  }

  .svc-timeline-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .svc-timeline-marker {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
  }

  .svc-timeline-day {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .svc-measure-card {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .svc-measure-card-final {
    border-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .svc-measure-heading {
    font-size: var(--size-xl);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .svc-measure-body {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .svc-measure-metrics {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .svc-measure-metrics li {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    position: relative;
  }

  .svc-measure-metrics li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: var(--weight-700);
  }

  .svc-measure-callout {
    background: var(--muted);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--primary);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-3);
  }

  .svc-measure-callout-text {
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--weight-600);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Capabilities ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .section-muted {
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  .svc-caps-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .svc-caps-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .svc-caps-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: baseline;
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    font-weight: var(--weight-500);
    color: var(--foreground);
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4);
